## How potentials that affect Us are changing, How can we test that ? Is it what we want exactly ? if we prove that there is a correlation  

Correlation between S and Tact : to separate 2 possible reasons, why uptake at one depth could change: the plant is asking for less water (demand), or the soil at that depth can't deliver it (local supply limitation)
If S follows Tact (same shape, constant proportion), then S changes only because demand changes. Nothing local is limiting it.
If S drops while Tact stays flat, the plant still pulls the same amount, but this depth delivers less. The limitation must be local, at the root–soil interface, and other depths are compensating.
